# Astral Wilds - protect Unreal binary assets from any line-ending/text
# conversion. Without this, a tool that touches these files with
# autocrlf-style conversion enabled could silently corrupt them. Added
# 2026-10-05 after a pure CRLF/LF churn was found on a source file
# (AstralAutoPlaytest.cpp) with no .gitattributes in place at all - the
# source churn itself was harmless, but the absence of any binary
# declaration for .uasset/.umap was not.
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# 2026-10-05: Unreal assets now stored in Git LFS (forward-only - history before
# this commit keeps them as plain blobs). -text keeps the binary protection above.
